WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.095 --> 00:00:05.434
- [Narrator] This is
Bermani, a martial eagle,

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.912
the largest African eagle.

00:00:07.912 --> 00:00:12.606
They have enough power in one
foot to break a human arm.

00:00:12.606 --> 00:00:15.109
As powerful as they are,
their strength in numbers

00:00:15.109 --> 00:00:18.483
continues to decrease in the wild.

00:00:18.483 --> 00:00:21.552
Martial eagles weigh
in at around 14 pounds,

00:00:21.552 --> 00:00:25.804
with a wingspan up to
eight and a half feet.

00:00:25.804 --> 00:00:28.411
Bermani is native to sub-Saharan Africa,

00:00:28.411 --> 00:00:31.755
preferring open woods, wooded savannah

00:00:31.755 --> 00:00:34.110
and thorn bush habitats.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.730
He is an apex predator, sitting at the top

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.366
of the avian food chain.

00:00:39.366 --> 00:00:43.398
Unfortunately, they are
being persecuted by humans,

00:00:43.398 --> 00:00:48.255
mistakenly believed to be a
predatory threat to livestock.

00:00:48.255 --> 00:00:50.979
In reality, domestic animals make up

00:00:50.979 --> 00:00:54.772
a very small percentage of their diet.

00:00:54.772 --> 00:00:58.319
Add to that a shrinking
habitat, which reduces prey,

00:00:58.319 --> 00:01:02.236
the martial eagle population
is dwindling fast.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.464
This is the martial eagle.

00:01:08.921 --> 00:01:11.588
(ambient tones)

